  "reviewed_behavior": [
    "The only new production integration replaces the shared empty-key map probe with default_namespace.is_none. Both direct and copied nonempty identity Starts call that helper; namespace-aware names under a default URI, colon spellings and xmlns attributes retain the expansion path.",
    "IdentityStartState neither reads nor owns the default URI. It borrows the prefix map only for its unchanged caller-salted hasher, while the source and disjoint mutation borrows end before raw publication and callback delivery. No new alias or retained source slice appears.",
    "The exact End branch remains after source accounting and position capture, before Start dispatch. It requires no local namespace undo scope and detaches the existing owned expanded name. A nested End under an inherited default may use it safely; declaring/undeclaring Ends retain scope undo and namespace callback order.",
    "Start lowering failures publish the complete current raw range before returning; account/scan failures and failed fallback token copies preserve old raw. Descriptor retention through native and Separate feeds, suspension and owned overrides is unchanged. Cold scratch after consecutive direct tokens can change later allocation ordinals without changing routing or checked limits.",
    "Default binding clone, context override, decoded-empty-prefix routing, reversed undo, deterministic serialization and logical key-plus-URI storage charge preserve their reviewed standalone implementation. The direct lowerer does not mutate namespace state.",
    "Declaration grammar/context/custom-map bootstrap merges without changes to its qualified implementation. Encoding/PI paths cannot satisfy completed planned Start or matched End guards. required_ascii-only proof excludes bytes custom maps may reinterpret; accepted custom release ownership and existing permissive TextDecl version grammar remain intact.",
    "Every standalone test function, including Start default-namespace negative control, source/raw/failure cases, End callback lifecycle, namespace salt/clone/budget cases and qualified custom-map declaration tests, survives byte-exact. Existing C-context full-record tests exercise the combined dispatch paths."
  ],
